                      VOID License 

This project contains original work created by simmrankumari24.  
The VOID License adds additional usage rules for the default branch.

1. Branch Protection  
   The default branch is protected.  
   Users may not fork, clone, or create derivative branches of the default branch. 

2. Contribution Method  
   Any changes, improvements, or fixes must be submitted as a pull request  
   directly to the default branch.  
   No other contribution paths are permitted.

3. Local Modifications  
   Users may create local copies for personal experimentation,  
   but these copies may not be published, pushed, or distributed  
   as separate branches or forks.

4. Public Distribution  
   Public redistribution of modified versions is only allowed  
   if the modifications were accepted into the default branch  
   through the pull request process.

